# Cloudflare Pages redirects. This file is copied verbatim to the site root by
# the Eleventy passthrough (src/static -> "."), so it lands at _site/_redirects
# where Pages reads it.
#
# The Stripe checkout/portal edge functions in openshore.code.ai
# (supabase/functions/stripe-checkout) default their success/cancel/portal
# return URLs to https://openshore.ai/os-code/ (?checkout=success on success),
# a holdover from when this page lived at openshore.ai/os-code/ on the
# Open-Shore-LLC-Homepage site. Now that OpenShore is the whole site at the
# root, keep that path alive as a redirect rather than editing and redeploying
# a live payments function; Cloudflare Pages forwards the query string, so
# ?checkout=success still reaches the page.
# Since 2026-11-16 /os-code/ is a page again: OS Code by OpenShore, the
# personal product's home, which carries the checkout runtime, so those
# return addresses land on it directly and need no rule here. (From
# 2026-11-07 to 2026-11-16 it redirected to /about/.)

# The site's layout since 2026-11-16 (founder): openshore.ai/ is OpenShore
# for Enterprise, /os-code/ is OS Code by OpenShore, the free personal coding
# agent, and the web app is /os-code/app/. Old addresses for the personal
# product and the old Enterprise page move with it.
/oscode           /os-code/       301
/oscode/          /os-code/       301
/os-code          /os-code/       301
/app              /os-code/app/   301
/app/             /os-code/app/   301
/enterprise       /               301
/enterprise/      /               301
# The page that sat at /about/ (the personal product's home, 2026-11-07 to
# 2026-11-16) is /os-code/ now, and the company About page was retired
# (founder, 2026-11-16).
/about            /os-code/       301
/about/           /os-code/       301

# Every page of OS Code by OpenShore lives under /os-code/ since 2026-11-16
# (founder: these pages belong to the personal product alone; OpenShore for
# Enterprise will get its own). They sat under /about/ from 2026-11-07 and at
# the root before that. Both old address families go straight to the page's
# home in one hop, so links on the web and the app builds already installed
# keep working. The root itself is NOT redirected: it is OpenShore for
# Enterprise. Since 2026-11-16 (founder) /privacy/, /terms/ and /support/ are
